# {{title}}

Generated by `ess generate ui --target react` from the `ess-ui/1` document `{{app}}`. Do not edit
the generated files; change the document and generate again.

## Run

```console
npm install
npm run dev
```

`npm run dev` serves the app at `http://127.0.0.1:5173`, bundling on each request. Every page
path is answered with `www/index.html`, so a reload or a link to any page opens the app.
`npm run build` type-checks and bundles into `www/assets/`; `npm run preview` serves the built
`www/` at `http://127.0.0.1:4173`. The only runtime dependencies are `react` and `react-dom`;
esbuild is the only build step.

Every read is answered from the document's fixtures and every live channel plays its fixture
script, so the application runs without a backend. To use a real one, call
`setDataAdapter(httpAdapter("<base url>"))` from `src/runtime/data.ts` and
`useNetworkChannels("<base url>")` from `src/runtime/live.ts` (when the document has channels)
before rendering, in `src/main.tsx`.

## Type-check

`npm run typecheck` checks against the real packages `npm install` brings.

`npm run typecheck:offline` (`tsc -p tsconfig.offline.json --noEmit`) checks without
`node_modules`: `tsconfig.offline.json` maps `react`, `react/jsx-runtime` and `react-dom/client`
onto the minimal declarations in `types/`. Once `npm install` has run, `tsconfig.json` uses the
real packages and `types/` is not read.

## Layout

| Path | What it is |
|---|---|
| `www/index.html` | the page every path is answered with; it loads `www/assets/main.js` and `main.css` |
| `src/App.tsx` | the router: the page a path matches, under its shell; any other path goes home |
| `src/routes.ts` | page paths, path matching and navigation |
| `src/shells/` | one component per shell, its regions, guards and state |
| `src/pages/` | one file per page: the page, one component per section, one per overlay |
| `src/model.ts` | the document's types |
| `src/fixtures.ts` | fixture rows per view and event scripts per channel |
| `src/channels.ts` | the document's channels and their transports |
| `src/runtime/` | the component set, the router, state placement, data adapter and live channels |

Every rendered node carries a `data-ui-path` attribute holding its canonical node path, so tests
select by path.
